    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s action with **Corbin Carroll** leading the charge, boasting an elite 77.46 score. His matchup against Rocker is our most favorable deployment, as the combination of a high-ceiling lineup spot and a positive platoon split makes him our top source for runs and speed. **James Wood** follows closely at 72.41, bolstered by his 0.415 xwOBA and a prime leadoff spot against Ure\u00f1a. While **Trevor Story** (68.70) and **Brice Turang** (67.90) remain solid starts, **Brice Turang**\u2019s efficiency is particularly notable; his 8% \"Order #2\" bonus and favorable SP skill metrics against Singer underscore our ongoing mandate to prioritize high-speed, high-OBP profiles to maintain our edge in the standings.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was benching **Isaac Paredes**, who missed the starting threshold by a slim margin (38.96 vs our 40.0 floor). Despite his solid base projection, a difficult matchup against Seymour and a severe -19% penalty for opposing pitcher skill pushed him out of the starting ten. Elsewhere, we are exercising caution with **Vinnie Pasquantino** (52.77) and **Austin Riley** (42.69); both are struggling with platoon disadvantages or elite opposing arms like Mayza, keeping their ceilings low. We are also monitoring **Josh Naylor** and **Cole Young**, as their scores are contingent on \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions; should the official cards show them batting lower than projected against Jump, those scores\u2014already hampered by the left-on-left dynamic\u2014could dip into the danger zone.",
